{
  "name": "SystemArchitecture",
  "internal_name": "SystemArchitecture",
  "focus": "High-level protocol boundaries and end-to-end control/data flow: users and external callers interact with account proxies through AccountManager; Registry, RiskEngine, OracleFacade, and LToken lending pools support account lifecycle, collateral and borrowing; ControllerFacade and protocol-specific controllers validate arbitrary DeFi interactions before Account.exec reaches external protocols; oracle adapters read external feeds and pool/vault data; Beacon and BeaconProxy provide account implementation routing and upgrades; deployment scripts wire the components.",
